# tests/e2e/fr060-business-home.spec.js writes this screenshot on every run, so a
# tracked copy makes `npm run test:e2e` dirty the working tree with binary churn
# that no document cites. The evidence is the passing spec, not the committed byte.
output/playwright/*.png
.env
*.local
__pycache__/
docs/v1-inherited/
# A nightly report template belonging to a different project (it names the repo
# robinbakshi007/ollama-direct-custom-agent and counts VS Code marketplace
# releases). Nothing here generates it; ignored so an external writer cannot
# reintroduce it as tracked noise.
JULES_REPORT.md

.vercel
_worktrees/

.vercel

.vercel
.env*

.vercel
.env*
# The template stays tracked; every other .env* (.env, .env.docker, ...) is private.
!.env.example

apps/server/src/generated/

# Written by apps/server/scripts/doc-graph.mjs on every regeneration, and read
# by nothing: the file's own note says it is "excluded from every
# staleness/consistency check by design", and a search for its path finds one
# writer and no reader. PR #278 introduced it to hold the drift diff that used
# to be baked into docs/.doc-graph.json, where it went stale against itself and
# failed `monorepo-graph.mjs --check` on fresh checkouts — the right fix, but
# tracked it carried a `generated_at` timestamp, so it conflicted on the very
# first merge after landing and would have on every one after. Untracked, the
# diagnostic still gets written and printed; only the merge churn goes away.
docs/.doc-graph-drift-report.json
